#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Non-Economists"
msgstr "Nie-ekonomiści"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A small team of researchers is woken up by their notification inboxes exploding: their mundane and unexciting report might have just started an economic war between multiple regions and communities. In a world with tightly-controlled carbon budgets, the production, use and recycling of every product is a subject of LCA, or a LifeCycle Assessment. A bad result might change the design, or move the production to another region, with potential political consequences. How will the researchers deal with their newly acquired (in)fame? Will they trust their analysis, buckle under pressure, or decide to play politics?\n"
msgstr "> Mały zespół badaczy zostaje nagle obudzony przez tysiące powiadomień: ich przyziemny i nudny raport być może właśnie rozpętał wojnę ekonomiczną pomiędzy kilkoma regionami i społecznościami. W świecie ściśle kontrolowanych budżetów węglowych produkcja, użytkowanie i recykling każdego produktu jest poddane LCA - Środowiskowej Ocenie Cyklu Życia. Zły wynik może wymusić przeprojektowanie - lub przenieść produkcję do innego regionu, z potencjalnymi konsekwencjami politycznymi. Jak ta grupa badaczy podoła swojej nowej (nie)sławie? Czy zaufają swoim obliczeniom, ugną się pod ciśnieniem, czy może zdecydują zacząć bawić się w politykę?\n"

#. type: Title ##
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Raw Research Notes"
msgstr "Notatki po angielsku"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"What we have then - whether in terms of Carbon Credits, LCAs or other "
"aspects - is a question how to structure a system to make sense and be "
"unhackable."
msgstr ""
"What we have then - whether in terms of Carbon Credits, LCAs or other "
"aspects - is a question how to structure a system to make sense and be "
"unhackable."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"One solution would be maximum transparency and treating the whole LCA "
"process: the knowledge base, algorithms, specific decisions as a wiki, where "
"everybody can look into and comment. How much can we offload on citizen "
"scientists and citizen economists, however?"
msgstr ""
"One solution would be maximum transparency and treating the whole LCA "
"process: the knowledge base, algorithms, specific decisions as a wiki, where "
"everybody can look into and comment. How much can we offload on citizen "
"scientists and citizen economists, however?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This will also lead to faction wars, both in terms of ideology and "
"economics. Every decision will have consequences - and even without layers "
"of red tape and sleazy CEOs people can be rallied to vote against something "
"important. What if the calculations show that - for example - India should "
"not produce steel, which could be picked up by another, much smaller "
"country? The sheer population and number of votes can out-weight it! Will "
"they then vote on a flawed calculation method, led by a demagogue?"
msgstr ""
"This will also lead to faction wars, both in terms of ideology and "
"economics. Every decision will have consequences - and even without layers "
"of red tape and sleazy CEOs people can be rallied to vote against something "
"important. What if the calculations show that - for example - India should "
"not produce steel, which could be picked up by another, much smaller "
"country? The sheer population and number of votes can out-weigh it! Will "
"they then vote on a flawed calculation method, led by a demagogue?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The bribes don't need to be financial. They can be prestige, acceptance by a "
"faction, or whatever else."
msgstr ""
"The bribes don't need to be financial. They can be prestige, acceptance by a "
"faction, or whatever else."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This prompt ties in with [the Miners](/seeds/the-miners), [The Moonshot](/"
"seeds/the-moonshot) and many others."
msgstr "This prompt ties in with the Miners, The Moonshot and many others."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Let's look for a story in it though:"
msgstr "Let's look for a story in it though:"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Let's imagine a group of LCA scientists who just published just another "
"analysis, being abruptly woken by their notification inboxes exploding. They "
"were just launched on the front lines of a faction war, where their report "
"was the \"last straw\" and might now contribute do a huge societal change, "
"removing whole sectors of economy from one region of the world into another. "
"Do they trust their work? Will they buckle under pressure? It's a good "
"opportunity to walk the reader through how the LCA process looks like."
msgstr ""
"Let's imagine a group of LCA scientists who just published just another "
"analysis, being abruptly woken by their notification inboxes exploding. They "
"were just launched on the front lines of a faction war, where their report "
"was the \"last straw\" and might now contribute do a huge societal change, "
"removing whole sectors of economy from one region of the world into another. "
"Do they trust their work? Will they buckle under pressure? It's a good "
"opportunity to walk the reader through how the LCA process looks like."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Consider the world to be more anarchist, less hierarchical, where a lot of "
"decisions are consensus-based and a subject of public debate, flames and "
"online brigading. The scientists behind this report are now celebrities, "
"widely known, whether they want it or not. If you want to cite a book with "
"similar themes, you can go with LX Beckett's \"Gamechanger\" or "
"\"Dealbreaker\", where the popular support for eco-policies is one of the "
"most important plots of both novels."
msgstr ""
"Consider the world to be more anarchist, less hierarchical, where a lot of "
"decisions are consensus-based and a subject of public debate, flames and "
"online brigading. The scientists behind this report are now celebrities, "
"widely known, whether they want it or not. If you want to cite a book with "
"similar themes, you can go with LX Beckett's \"Gamechanger\" or "
"\"Dealbreaker\", where the popular support for eco-policies is one of the "
"most important plots of both novels."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Let's remember that more and more LCA processes are not just about energy "
"and material, but are trying to count-in the uncountable, the effects on "
"human happiness and labour practices. Yes, we could move the industry to "
"China, but the general economic effect will produce X more tons of CO2, even "
"if the factories will be more efficient."
msgstr ""
"Let's remember that more and more LCA processes are not just about energy "
"and material, but are trying to count-in the uncountable, the effects on "
"human happiness and labour practices. Yes, we could move the industry to "
"China, but the general economic effect will produce X more tons of CO2, even "
"if the factories will be more efficient."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Original notes:"
msgstr "Original notes:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"If they aren’t careful, they could become like the economists of the past "
"centuries, worshiping a mathematical model and a paradigm, instead of "
"continuously testing it."
msgstr ""
"If they aren’t careful, they could become like the economists of the past "
"centuries, worshiping a mathematical model and a paradigm, instead of "
"continuously testing it."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Struggles of morality are ongoing in solarpunk"
msgstr "Struggles of morality are ongoing in solarpunk"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Sources:"
msgstr "Sources:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life-cycle_assessment"
msgstr "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life-cycle_assessment"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"We can throw in the https://globalcarbonreward.org/ and let's say, \"good "
"faith\", non-blockchain carbon counting systems. We WILL need one."
msgstr ""
"We can throw in the https://globalcarbonreward.org/ and let's say, \"good "
"faith\", non-blockchain carbon counting systems. We WILL need one."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Pharmacists"
msgstr "Farmakolodzy"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A motley collection of neo-archeologists, data experts, doctors and biohackers are going through databases of the fallen pharmaceutical corporations, looking for drugs and solutions which worked, but were too cheap for the company giants to market. With so many medicines and procedures gone or extremely hard to get, maybe this is the best chance to rediscover cures?\n"
msgstr "> Barwna gromadka neoarcheologów, ekspertów od danych, lekarzy i biohakerów przeszukuje bazy danych upadłych korporacji farmaceutycznych w poszukiwaniu leków i rozwiązań, które działały, ale były zbyt tanie, by kapitalistyczni giganci chcieli je wprowadzić na rynek. Skoro tak wiele leków i procedur przestało istnieć lub jest niezwykle trudno dostępnych, może to jest właśnie najlepsza szansa na znalezienie nowych lekarstw?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/"
"@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-pharmacists)"
msgstr ""
"[Odcinek Podcastu Solarpunk Prompts](https://podcast.tomasino.org/"
"@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-pharmacists)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
msgid ""
"[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-"
"Pharmacists)"
msgstr ""
"[Transkrypt](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-"
"Pharmacists)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Priorities"
msgstr "Priorytety"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A team of architects and civil engineers working on future-proofing their community need to make a hard decision. They are trying to prioritize the threats, but it’s a gamble trying to balance effectiveness and accessibility. They could make sure that one block won’t get flooded, but another district would need to wait.\n"
msgstr "> Zespół architektów i inżynierów pracujących nad uodpornieniem miasta na przyszłe katastrofy musi podejmować trudne decyzje i ryzykować, ustalając priorytety zagrożeń. Ich największym, rozdzierającym serce wyzwaniem jest wyważenie skuteczności i dostępności ich rozwiązania. Jasne, mogą sprawić, że nikt z tej przecznicy nie zostanie zalany, ale druga połowa dzielnicy będzie musiała pocierpieć.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Continuing the architecture and infrastructure again, this time from the "
"perspective of the architects. This can be a pre-solarpunk or solarpunk "
"endeavor, shown as more reactionary in the chaos of everything, or more of a "
"\"good practice\" after decades of notes and hard decisions already made."
msgstr ""
"Continuing the architecture and infrastructure again, this time from the "
"perspective of the architects. This can be a pre-solarpunk or solarpunk "
"endeavor, shown as more reactionary in the chaos of everything, or more of a "
"\"good practice\" after decades of notes and hard decisions already made."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This is NOT a crisis response team. The flood, the heatwave, the hurricane "
"are not here yet. You are to make them less threatening, not start "
"evacuating people right now."
msgstr ""
"This is NOT a crisis response team. The flood, the heatwave, the hurricane "
"are not here yet. You are to make them less threatening, not start "
"evacuating people right now."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The \"accessibility\" means three things: access of an average citizen to "
"the infrastructure (a shelter maybe?), access of poorer / less fortunate "
"residents to protenctions in their district, and of course access of the "
"disabled citizens to things they need, as wheelchair-bound people will "
"really struggle with knee-high floods."
msgstr ""
"The \"accessibility\" means three things: access of an average citizen to "
"the infrastructure (a shelter maybe?), access of poorer / less fortunate "
"residents to protenctions in their district, and of course access of the "
"disabled citizens to things they need, as wheelchair-bound people will "
"really struggle with knee-high floods."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Will this mean abandoning districts and forcible relocations, or worse, "
"climate ghettos?"
msgstr ""
"Will this mean abandoning districts and forcible relocations, or worse, "
"climate ghettos?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Assuming the team has access to all the required data, scientists, "
"meteorologists, city archives: how many different kinds of climate threats "
"can they protect us from? What will help with heatwaves, what with floods, "
"hurricanes?"
msgstr ""
"Assuming the team has access to all the required data, scientists, "
"meteorologists, city archives: how many different kinds of climate threats "
"can they protect us from? What will help with heatwaves, what with floods, "
"hurricanes?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"What prices are considered too steep to pay? Are we going to surrender "
"historical sites, places of remembrance? Are we okay with destroying a flood "
"shaft and flooding a nature reserve to protect the population?"
msgstr ""
"What prices are considered too steep to pay? Are we going to surrender "
"historical sites, places of remembrance? Are we okay with destroying a flood "
"shaft and flooding a nature reserve to protect the population?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"How does the background of the team members play into that? Who already "
"lives in a \"safe\", sutstainable tower, radiating pride and confidence, who "
"clings to their family house in the suburbs, who cannot afford leaving a "
"dangerous building which will not survive the next cataclysm?"
msgstr ""
"How does the background of the team members play into that? Who already "
"lives in a \"safe\", sutstainable tower, radiating pride and confidence, who "
"clings to their family house in the suburbs, who cannot afford leaving a "
"dangerous building which will not survive the next cataclysm?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"What time-scale are we talking about? Are we okay with cheaper protections "
"that will last a year, are we going for 5 years, a decade, or more?"
msgstr ""
"What time-scale are we talking about? Are we okay with cheaper protections "
"that will last a year, are we going for 5 years, a decade, or more?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"How do we communicate it to the population, not to appear as despots "
"choosing one group over another?"
msgstr ""
"How do we communicate it to the population, not to appear as despots "
"choosing one group over another?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"What if we fail, what if we prepared for a flood and an unexpected heatwave "
"rolls over, killing thousands? How do team members deal with guilt, do they "
"accept the blame? Deny it?"
msgstr ""
"What if we fail, what if we prepared for a flood and an unexpected heatwave "
"rolls over, killing thousands? How do team members deal with guilt, do they "
"accept the blame? Deny it?"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A good book on the social infrastructure and the challenges of urban "
"planning: https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/37707827 , with some tl;dr "
"in https://99percentinvisible.org/episode/palaces-for-the-people/"
msgstr ""
"A good book on the social infrastructure and the challenges of urban "
"planning: https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/37707827 , with some tl;dr "
"in https://99percentinvisible.org/episode/palaces-for-the-people/"

